      "title": "ServiceNow: The Burning Platform Nobody Is Burning",
      "fund": "Substack / Cheap Software Stocks",
      "date": "April 14, 2026",
      "summary": "Presents a deep-dive underwrite arguing that ServiceNow ($NOW) is severely mispriced due to narrative-driven AI disruption panic . Highlights that NOW's Configuration Management Database (CMDB) serves as irreplaceable enterprise context, positioning the company as the primary governance landlord for autonomous AI agents. Notes strong fundamentals ($13.3B trailing revenue, $4.6B FCF, and guidance for ~20% subscription growth) alongside a massive $10B cash balance providing significant downside protection.",
      "url": "https://cheapsoftwarestocks.substack.com/p/servicenow-the-burning-platform-nobody",
      "btn_label": "Substack Memo \u2197"
    },
    {
      "title": "ServiceNow 1Q26: More Control, Less Conviction",
      "fund": "Substack / Nikhs",
      "date": "April 22, 2026",
      "summary": "Analyzes ServiceNow's structural transition into the governance control tower for enterprise AI workflows, with non-seat usage-based pricing reaching 50% of net new business. Evaluates management's record $2.2B accelerated share repurchase alongside operational execution risks as rising AI compute costs pressure gross margins. Concludes that while the architectural moat as enterprise AI's control plane is strengthening, sustained valuation expansion requires organic revenue reacceleration and gross margin floor stabilization.",
      "url": "https://nikhs.substack.com/archive?sort=search&search=NOW",
      "btn_label": "Substack Memo \u2197"
    },
    {
      "title": "ServiceNow \u2013 The Market Is Selling a Narrative, The Numbers Tell a Different Story",
      "fund": "Substack / Rijnberk InvestInsights",
      "date": "July 25, 2026",
      "summary": "Reevaluates ServiceNow following strong Q2 results (subscription revenue +23% FX-neutral to $3.88B and total RPO up 21% to $29B), concluding that market pessimism has disconnected the stock price from operational momentum. Details a fair value price target of $218 per share (~26% implied CAGR) anchored on long-term contract expansion, sticky retention rates, and valuation multiple re-rating from compressed 16-17x FCF levels. Identifies accelerating enterprise deal sizes and rapid AI product adoption as key operational catalysts.",
      "url": "https://substack.com/search/NOW%20ServiceNow%2C%20Inc.%20investment%20thesis",
      "btn_label": "Substack Search \u2197"
    },
    {
      "title": "Why ServiceNow may be one of the most mispriced stocks today",
      "fund": "r/ValueInvesting",
      "date": "April 07, 2026",
      "summary": "Focuses on the market disconnect between ServiceNow's 97% recurring subscription model ($13.28B FY2025 revenue) and the aggressive sector-wide sell-off in SaaS equities. Argues that industry-leading gross margins, high multi-product cross-selling penetration, and near-perfect customer retention prove deep switching costs that shield the business from raw LLM disruption. Contends that current market pricing overlooks the critical nature of sticky IT workflow infrastructure, creating a compelling value setup.",
      "url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/ValueInvesting/search/?q=NOW&restrict_sr=1&sort=top",
